// endpoint_update_persistent_wifi_mode.proto — UpdatePersistentWifiMode: turn
// the host machine's persistent wifi mode (lid-closed operation) on, off, or
// over. HOST MACHINE section. Daemon-scoped: nothing here names a workspace,
// and Emacs calls it over its one daemon-level connection.
//
// THE CHANGE RUNS IN THIS ORDER, and the order is the contract:
//   1. the hotspot — joined when turning on, left when turning off — FIRST, so
//      the network is settled before anything else;
//   2. the power settings — sleep disabled (on) or enabled (off), together
//      with network-over-sleep and wake-on-network — the one step that
//      decides whether the change happened at all;
//   3. the display — dimmed (on) or restored (off) — LAST, as the visible
//      sign that the machine is in its final state and the lid may close.
// A failed hotspot or display step never stops the power step: staying awake
// on whatever network is present is still the outcome asked for, so those two
// steps report how they went inside the SUCCESS, and only a refused power step
// is a failure.

